t `to-review` as the accepted handoff for the orchestrator to checkpoint and make the `done` transition. No `commit_ack` was supplied by this run.\n\n**What I attacked**\n\n- The gate is a single depth counter in the shared strict decoder, and every public entry hits that decoder first. I confirmed no other decoder in the package can see peer bytes. The JSON re-encode and JCS transform only run on the already bounded value.\n- I ran four mutants myself and restored the tree after each: widen to 512, widen to 257, narrow to 128, and delete the gate. All four redden the suite. The delete-gate mutant reproduces the exact original crash, a fatal goroutine stack overflow from the 2 MB regression input.\n- The tests pin the literal 256 in the test file rather than reading the constant, so narrowing fails the accept-at-limit tests and widening fails the refuse-past-limit tests. Both directions are covered at all three public entries in array, object, and mixed container shapes.\n- The identity at-limit proof is indirect but sound. The refusal comes from the later Section 1.6 extension depth gate, which is unreachable unless the decoder accepted the 256-deep document.\n\n**Gates I reran on the candidate tree**\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `go test ./... -count=1 -cover` | exit 0 |\n| build, vet, gofmt | clean |\n| tracecheck full and sections 1.6 + 10.1 | ok, repinned ownership digest verifies |\n| cataloggen check | exit 0 |\n| canonicaljson coverage vs base 48db30b | 87.1% to 87.2%, other packages unchanged |\n| `git verify-commit HEAD` | good signature |\n\n**Board state**\n\n- Verdict artifact attached as `BUG-260902-lyhvkw_review-verdict.md`, with mutant and gate logs under `.temp/BUG-260902-lyhvkw-review/`.\n- Definition of Done items 13 through 18 checked. The list has 18 items, so my attempt to check a nineteenth was a harmless range error.\n- One residual note, not blocking: a stray closing delimiter at depth 256 would be reported as a depth error rather than an unexpected delimiter. Both are the same typed error and the standard decoder refuses mismatched delimiters first, so this path is unreachable.","ttft_ms":3023,"type":"result","duration_ms":264055,"uuid":"5b2a7e46-232d-4f4c-b116-ebf78582fe51","ttft_stream_ms":2607,"time_to_request_ms":21,"queued_turn_count":0}
